      "readme": "# A comprehensive physiological dataset of pain and aversive modalities for pain biomarkers research \n\nThis dataset contains EEG recordings from 125 pain-free adults, as well as galvanic skin response and electrocardiogram data in a subset of 76 participants, from two resting-state and four experimental conditions (thermal and chemical pain; aversive auditory and taste stimulations). Behavioural, sociodemographic, and psychological data are also available in the participants.tsv file. \n\nThis work was funded by the *Fonds de Recherche du Québec - Santé (FRQS)*, the *Fonds de Recherche du Québec - Nature et technologie (FRQNT)*, the *Réseau de bio-imagerie du Québec (RBIQ)*, the *Natural Sciences and Engineering Research Council of Canada (CRSNG)*, and the *Canadian Pain Society (CPS)*. \n\nFor full details on the dataset and study design, please refer to the related publication. \n\nThe code used to process and analyze the data is publicly available at XXX.\n\n## Related publication\n\nChampagne, A., Barrette, L.-È., Cyr-Bouchard, A., Roy, M., & Coll., M.-P. ([Year]). A comprehensive physiological dataset of pain and aversive modalities for pain biomarkers research. [*Journal name*], [*Volume*]([Issue]), [Page range]. [DOI or URL]\n\n### Notes\n\nNotes and comments specific to a given participant (e.g., behaviour during data collection, technical issues, or other participant-specific information) are documented in the participants.tsv file. \n\n",
